  <Placemark>
   <name>Storm Warning issued November 14 at 12:38PM PST until November 15 at 4:00AM PST by NWS Portland OR</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_severe</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>* WHAT...For the first Hazardous Seas Warning, very steep and
hazardous seas 18 to 23 ft at 17 seconds and south winds 25 to
35 kt with gusts up to 40 kt. For the Storm Warning, seas 16
to 21 ft at 15 seconds and south winds 30 to 40 kt with gusts
up to 50 kt expected. For the second Hazardous Seas Warning,
very steep and hazardous seas 17 to 22 ft at 17 seconds and
south winds 20 to 30 kt with gusts up to 35 kt expected.

* WHERE...Inner Coastal Waters from Cape Shoalwater to Florence
out 10 NM.

* WHEN...Hazardous Seas Warning, until 4 PM PST this afternoon.
Storm Warning, from 4 PM this afternoon to 4 AM PST Sunday.
Hazardous Seas Warning, from 4 AM Sunday to 4 AM PST Monday.

* IMPACTS...Very strong winds will cause hazardous seas which
could capsize or damage vessels and reduce visibility.</Snippet>
