  <Placemark>
   <name>Flood Watch issued November 14 at 12:05PM PST until November 15 at 10:00AM PST by NWS Seattle WA</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_severe</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be
possible.

* WHERE...A portion of northwest Washington, including the following
county, Mason.

* WHEN...Through Sunday morning.

* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,
creeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- Two to four inches of rain is forecast for the south slopes of
the Olympics through Sunday morning with snow levels of 5000 to
6000 feet. The combination of heavy rain and relatively high snow
levels could push the Skokomish River near Potlatch above flood
stage.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood</Snippet>
