  <Placemark>
   <name>Small Craft Advisory issued November 14 at 10:17AM CST until November 15 at 6:00PM CST by NWS Corpus Christi TX</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_minor</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>* WHAT...For the Small Craft Advisory, southeast winds 15 to 25
knots with gusts up to 30 knots and seas 5 to 8 feet expected.
For the Gale Watch, northeast winds 20 to 30 knots with gusts
up to 35 knots and seas 8 to 13 feet possible.

* WHERE...Baffin Bay and Upper Laguna Madre, Corpus Christi and
Nueces Bays, Copano, Aransas, and Redfish Bays, San Antonio,
Mesquite, and Espiritu Santo Bays, Coastal waters from Baffin
Bay to Port Aransas out 20 NM, Coastal waters from Port
Aransas to Matagorda Ship Channel out 20 NM, Waters from
Baffin Bay to Port Aransas from 20 to 60 NM and Waters from
Port Aransas to Matagorda Ship Channel from 20 to 60 NM.

* WHEN...For the Small Craft Advisory, from 4 PM this afternoon
to 6 PM CST Sunday. For the Gale Watch, from Sunday evening
through Monday afternoon.

* IMPACTS...Gale force winds and high seas will result in
dangerous marine conditions which could result in capsized or
damaged vessels.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...The small craft advisory may be extended
for the bays beyond Sunday night dependent on the decision for
an upgrade for the Gale Watch.</Snippet>
