  <Placemark>
   <name>Hazardous Seas Warning issued November 14 at 2:08AM PST until November 14 at 1:00PM PST by NWS Medford OR</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_moderate</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>* WHAT...For the Hazardous Seas Warning, very steep and hazardous
seas 25 to 30 ft at 18 seconds. For the Storm Warning, south
winds 35 to 45 kt with gusts up to 60 kt and chaotic, very
steep, hazardous seas 19 to 24 ft expected.

* WHERE...All the area.

* WHEN...For the Hazardous Seas Warning, until 1 PM PST this
afternoon. For the Storm Warning, from 1 PM Saturday to 1 AM
PST Sunday.

* IMPACTS...Very strong winds and very steep seas could capsize
or damage vessels. Visibilities will be significantly reduced.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Following this afternoon and tonight's
strong front, another round of very high westerly swell, peaking
at 20 to 25 feet at 16 seconds will move in Sunday into Monday.
Please continue to monitor the forecast for updates on this
high impact weather pattern.</Snippet>
